GRAPH <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Digest_Narrative_ZypherionAnalyticsAdoption> {
  <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Digest_Narrative_ZypherionAnalyticsAdoption> a narr:Digest ;
    narr:digestOf <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Narrative_ZypherionAnalyticsAdoption> ;
    narr:childCount "5"^^xsd:integer ;
    narr:generatedFrom "f8f9adee1745fc9e816ab87bf3a33713d20b2dca" ;
    narr:narration """This hub traces the reversal of Zypherion's analytics adoption and the pivot to Meridian, all dated 20260707. The original case for Zypherion rested on a [15x columnar query performance advantage](narr:https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Claim_ZypherionColumnarPerformance), which drove the initial adoption decision. That rationale was overturned when CTO Quinton Fairweather's further evaluation surfaced [critical streaming ingestion gaps](narr:https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Claim_ZypherionStreamingGap) — identified as the decisive factor in reversing course. Meridian was selected as the replacement on the strength of [native batch and streaming ingestion capability](narr:https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Claim_MeridianBatchStreamingNative). The Q3 2026 migration window was preserved: [Meridian's migration is scheduled for the same Q3 2026 window originally planned for Zypherion](narr:https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Claim_MeridianMigrationTimeline), with [Zypherion's superseded timeline](narr:https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Claim_ZypherionMigrationTimeline) still present as a reference point. The graph holds the full arc — original rationale, reversal trigger, replacement selection, and continuity of schedule — without resolving whether the columnar advantage remains relevant under Meridian.""" ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Claim_MeridianBatchStreamingNative> ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Claim_MeridianMigrationTimeline> ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Claim_ZypherionColumnarPerformance> ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Claim_ZypherionMigrationTimeline> ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Claim_ZypherionStreamingGap> ;
    narr:keyPhrase [ narr:text "15x columnar query performance advantage was the original rationale for adoption" ; narr:phraseSource <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Claim_ZypherionColumnarPerformance> ] ;
    narr:keyPhrase [ narr:text "critical gaps in streaming ingestion, as identified by CTO Quinton Fairweather during further evaluation" ; narr:phraseSource <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Claim_ZypherionStreamingGap> ] ;
    narr:keyPhrase [ narr:text "decisive factor in reversing the adoption decision" ; narr:phraseSource <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Claim_ZypherionStreamingGap> ] ;
    narr:keyPhrase [ narr:text "handles both batch and streaming ingestion natively" ; narr:phraseSource <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Claim_MeridianBatchStreamingNative> ] ;
    narr:keyPhrase [ narr:text "Q3 2026 window originally planned for Zypherion" ; narr:phraseSource <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Claim_MeridianMigrationTimeline> ] ;
    narr:variation [ narr:text "Zypherion's 15x columnar performance advantage was never refuted on its own terms — only displaced by the streaming gap; it remains a live consideration if streaming requirements change or Meridian's columnar performance is later questioned." ; narr:over <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Claim_ZypherionColumnarPerformance> ; narr:over <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Claim_ZypherionStreamingGap> ] ;
    narr:variation [ narr:text "Two children describe the Q3 2026 migration window under different framings — one Meridian-forward, one anchored to the superseded Zypherion plan — leaving open whether the schedule continuity is incidental or a deliberate constraint." ; narr:over <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Claim_MeridianMigrationTimeline> ; narr:over <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Claim_ZypherionMigrationTimeline> ] ;
    narr:variation [ narr:text "The superseded Zypherion adoption claim carries both 'supports' and 'challenges' predicates, marking it as a still-present counter-signal rather than a cleanly archived dead end." ; narr:over <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Claim_ZypherionColumnarPerformance> ] ;
    narr:writer "anthropic/claude-sonnet-4.6" .
}